{#
  The crowdsec-jobs sidecar's identity. The remote allowlist and the home allowlist call the
  Kubernetes API; the other two jobs run cscli alone. Its rules are the grant set the H2 plan's
  *CrowdSec* derives from the calls remote_allowlist.py makes, less the exec grant the sidecar
  replaces, and the one read home_allowlist.py makes:

    logs deploy/traefik -c access-log-rotate   get on deployments.apps, list on pods,
                                               get on pods/log, in homelab
    get ingressroute -A                        get and list on ingressroutes.traefik.io,
                                               cluster-wide
    get configmap crowdsec-home-ips            get on that one ConfigMap, in homelab

  The ClusterRole is cluster-wide because routes live in three namespaces. Narrowing the read
  to homelab would change which routers count as authelia-gated, so the grant follows the
  script.

  `pods/log` cannot name the Traefik pod, whose name changes on every rollout, so the grant
  reads every homelab pod's log. That is why the token reaches the sidecar alone, through a
  projected volume, and never the engine container (deployment.yaml.j2).
  ansible/tests/k8s/test_rbac_against_script.py runs each module's main with a recording runner
  and holds these rules to the calls it records.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: crowdsec-jobs
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
automountServiceAccountToken: false
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: crowdsec-jobs
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
rules:
  - apiGroups: [apps]
    resources: [deployments]
    verbs: [get]
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: [pods]
    verbs: [list]
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: [pods/log]
    verbs: [get]
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: [configmaps]
    verbs: [get]
    resourceNames: [{{ crowdsec_k8s_home_ips_configmap }}]
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: crowdsec-jobs
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
roleRef:
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
  kind: Role
  name: crowdsec-jobs
subjects:
  - kind: ServiceAccount
    name: crowdsec-jobs
    namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: crowdsec-jobs
rules:
  - apiGroups: [traefik.io]
    resources: [ingressroutes]
    verbs: [get, list]
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: crowdsec-jobs
roleRef:
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: crowdsec-jobs
subjects:
  - kind: ServiceAccount
    name: crowdsec-jobs
    namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
